RESOLUTION NO.____
Date:...f/(,
I
ENTITLED: “A RESOLUTION ACKNOWLEDGING RECEIPT OF THE ARCHER
TRAIL CONNECTOR PLAN.”
WHEREAS, the Cheyenne Metropolitan Planning Organization (MPO) retained Ayres
Associates on June 29, 201$ to produce the Archer Trail Connector Plan (Plan); and
WHEREAS, the Plan explores options to connect the existing Cheyenne Greenway, that
ends at the intersection of HR Ranch Road and Campstool Road, to the Laramie County Archer
Complex; and
WHEREAS, to solicit and receive public input on options for the Cheyenne Greenway or
trails to connect to existing and future segments in Southeast Cheyenne, MPO staff and Ayres
Associates were at the Laramie County Fair
— Archer Complex at various times from July 30
—
August 2, 2018; and
WhEREAS, additionally, a public meeting was held at the Fire Training facility on
January 29, 2019 and an on-line survey was prepared and open for several weeks; and
WHEREAS, a project steering committee consisting of staff from the Wyoming
Department of Transportation (WYDOT), City of Cheyenne Planning Department, Laramie
County Public Works, City of Cheyenne Community Recreation & Events, Cheyenne MPO, a
Laramie County Commissioner, and a citizen member of the Cheyenne Greenway Advisory
Committee, met three times; and
WHEREAS, the Plan recommends Cheyenne Greenway and companion/independent
soft surface trail plans and profiles at a 35% planning level from the intersection of Campstool
Road and HR Ranch Road; and
WHEREAS, the Plan also recommends on-street bike lanes for road cyclists from the
Christensen Railroad Overpass Project to the north side of the Archer Complex along existing
roadways; and
WHEREAS, the Cheyenne MPO Citizen’s Advisory and Technical Committee reviewed
the Plan and recommended approval to the MPO Policy Committee; and
WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne Planning Commission held a Public Meeting on June
17, 2019, and accepted public comments, and recommended the approval of the plan to the City
of Cheyenne Governing Body.
1
